# The font packages `playwright-core install --with-deps --only-shell chromium` adds to a GitHub
# `ubuntu-24.04` runner. The portal image installs them the same way
# (deploy/base-images/portal-ai/Dockerfile), so CI prints its PDFs with the font set production
# has. Every Chromium shared library, fonts-liberation and fonts-noto-color-emoji are already in
# the runner image.
#
# `.github/scripts/stage-chromium-fonts.sh stage` downloads THESE packages, extracts their files
# (no dpkg install) and packs them as the `chromium-fonts` cache. A shard unpacks that cache
# instead of reaching an Ubuntu mirror (Doc/Architecture/ReadingCiSignals, "A cancelled shard
# can be a bad assignment"). On a cache miss, `stage` first checks this list against what the
# pinned Playwright asks for on the runner's release, and fails naming any font package that is
# neither listed here nor already installed.
#
# xfonts-encodings and xfonts-utils are the dependencies apt pulls in for xfonts-cyrillic and
# xfonts-scalable.
fonts-freefont-ttf
fonts-ipafont-gothic
fonts-tlwg-loma-otf
fonts-unifont
fonts-wqy-zenhei
xfonts-cyrillic
xfonts-encodings
xfonts-scalable
xfonts-utils
